\The book returns to the middle of the table. #id:line.Day1.result.E.007
\The reply comes before the place is found. #id:line.Day1.result.E.008
\Lavinia, message\: Tomorrow, then. Finish your date. #id:line.Day1.result.E.009
\The phone goes face down. #id:line.Day1.result.E.010
\Someone is listening. I know it without knowing where to look. #id:line.Day1.result.E.011
\You can wait. #id:line.Day1.result.E.012
\“What did she say?” Sylvia asks. #id:line.Day1.result.E.013
\“To finish.” #id:line.Day1.result.E.014
\“Very sensible.” #id:line.Day1.result.E.015
\Sylvia gives back the man's part. The man has been asked to read the eulogy. #id:line.Day1.result.E.016
\“With the flowers still in her lap?” #id:line.Day1.result.E.017
\“Apparently.” Sylvia turns the page. “Wait. I want to hear this.” #id:line.Day1.result.E.018
\She reaches across to point out a sentence and knocks the spoon onto the saucer; my hand moves the cup so that she can leave her wrist on the page. #id:line.Day1.result.E.019
\I missed this line before. #id:line.Day1.result.E.020
\“‘Her absence,’ I read, ‘will leave a silence—’” #id:line.Day1.result.E.021
\“‘Louder,’ said the aunt.” #id:line.Day1.result.E.022
\We continue until Sylvia puts the book down of her own accord. #id:line.Day1.result.E.023
\“Enough?” #id:line.Day1.result.E.024
\“One more.” #id:line.Day1.result.E.025
\“One.” #id:line.Day1.result.E.026
\She reads the woman's answer; my eyes stay on her until she has finished. At the stairs, Sylvia puts the paperback in her bag and says the man's voice is ruined for her now. #id:line.Day1.result.E.027
\“You can do him differently.” #id:line.Day1.result.E.028
\“I don't want to now.” #id:line.Day1.result.E.029
\She goes down before an answer can follow. #id:line.Day1.result.E.030
\Evening. Alone at the desk when the call goes through to Lavinia. There is no video. #id:line.Day1.result.E.031
\“You could have waited until tomorrow,” Lavinia says. #id:line.Day1.result.E.032
\“Would you rather I had?” #id:line.Day1.result.E.033
\“No.” The chair tilts back from the desk. #id:line.Day1.result.E.034
label Day1.result.E.next
return

label Day1.coda
\A zip runs close to Lavinia's microphone. #id:line.Day1.coda.001
\“Hold on.” #id:line.Day1.coda.002
\Something scrapes. She breathes out sharply. #id:line.Day1.coda.003
\“Too much?” I ask. #id:line.Day1.coda.004
\“For the case.” #id:line.Day1.coda.005
\“Take something out.” #id:line.Day1.coda.006
\“I want it.” #id:line.Day1.coda.007
\A corner of the mouth lifts in the quiet room. #id:line.Day1.coda.008
\She tries the zip again. #id:line.Day1.coda.009
\“What are you taking?” #id:line.Day1.coda.010
\“I haven't decided what I'm leaving.” #id:line.Day1.coda.011
\“That's going well.” #id:line.Day1.coda.012
\“Very.” #id:line.Day1.coda.013
\For a while the line carries only the sound of her moving things. Once she laughs at something unseen. #id:line.Day1.coda.014
\“What?” #id:line.Day1.coda.015
\“Nothing.” #id:line.Day1.coda.016
\“That was a laugh.” #id:line.Day1.coda.017
\“Yes.” #id:line.Day1.coda.018
\Silence waits for her to continue. #id:line.Day1.coda.019
\“You'll see tomorrow,” she says. #id:line.Day1.coda.020
\After a moment, the zip closes. #id:line.Day1.coda.021
\“There.” #id:line.Day1.coda.022
\The chair turns back toward the desk. #id:line.Day1.coda.023
\“Stay on the call.” #id:line.Day1.coda.024
\“I've finished.” #id:line.Day1.coda.025
\“I know.” #id:line.Day1.coda.026
\A faint knock comes through the phone. #id:line.Day1.coda.027
\“Priscilla.” #id:line.Day1.coda.028
\“Yes?” #id:line.Day1.coda.029
\“You don't have to stay.” #id:line.Day1.coda.030
\“Would you like me to go?” #id:line.Day1.coda.031
\“I asked if you wanted to.” #id:line.Day1.coda.032
\“No.” #id:line.Day1.coda.033
\“All right.” #id:line.Day1.coda.034
\The phone comes a little closer to the chin; something brushes against the microphone. #id:line.Day1.coda.035
\“Put it down,” Lavinia says. “I can hear you moving it.” #id:line.Day1.coda.036
\It settles flat beside the lamp. #id:line.Day1.coda.037
\“Like that?” #id:line.Day1.coda.038
\“Yes.” #id:line.Day1.coda.039
\The desk is lit in a small circle; the rest of the room is dark. #id:line.Day1.coda.040
\“Don't hang up when I stop talking,” Lavinia says. #id:line.Day1.coda.041
\“I wasn't going to.” #id:line.Day1.coda.042
\She asks what was so funny about the book. #id:line.Day1.coda.043
\“She keeps stopping her own funeral.” #id:line.Day1.coda.044
\“Is she dead?” #id:line.Day1.coda.045
\“She's practising.” #id:line.Day1.coda.046
\Into the quiet room, in the aunt's voice\: “‘Again. You sound relieved.’” #id:line.Day1.coda.047
\The laugh comes through the phone, then a rustle. #id:line.Day1.coda.048
\When she becomes quiet, the phone stays where it is. #id:line.Day1.coda.049
label Day1.coda.next
return

